     "text": "Khwaja Hasan Nizami’s full name was Syed Ali Hasan Nizami, while Allama Iqbal gave him the name Khwaja Hasan Nizami and he became famous by that name. He was born in the settlement of the shrine of Hazrat Khwaja Nizamuddin Auliya, three miles from Delhi. Khwaja Sahib was only eleven years old when his parents passed away. His elder brother brought him up. Khwaja Sahib opened his eyes in an environment where Sufism reigned. Along with the prevalent sciences he also received education in Sufism. Through the company of Munshi Ghulam Nizamuddin (a bookseller of Delhi) a literary taste and a journalistic inclination developed in him. He wrote his first essay under the title “India’s Delicate Condition”. Then for some time he wrote for magazines named “Paisa”, “Wakeel” and “Makhzan”. To promote the aims of the “Halqa-e-Nizam-ul-Mashaikh” he travelled in 1911 to Egypt, Syria, Palestine, Arabia and other Islamic countries. In 1919 he launched his first monthly magazine under the title “Nizam-ul-Mashaikh”. At various times he wrote several hundred books and pamphlets, small and large.",
