     "text": "Behind him came a king, on whose head was the Kayanian cap and over it the Kaviani banner swayed, but its flag was torn to shreds. He came slowly, as if protecting his wound. His colour was pale and he hung his head in shame. When he came, Alexander rose with great dignity to receive him and seated him beside himself. In spite of this, the more Alexander honoured him, the greater his shame grew. He was Darius, king of Iran.",
