   "content": "<p>Exercise</p><p>1. Fill in the blanks.</p><p>(a) The rhythm of his heart was ________ .</p><p>(b) The patient has a heart ailment which is called ________ .</p><p>(c) He was conscious and could take stock of his ________ .</p><p>(d) He looked towards Manzoor with ________ eyes.</p><p>(e) In his eyes Manzoor&#x27;s person had the rank of a ________ .</p><p>2. Write answers to the following questions.</p><p>(a) In what condition was Akhtar brought to the hospital?</p><p>(b) What was the cause of Manzoor&#x27;s illness?</p><p>(c) Why did Manzoor not want to go home from the hospital?</p><p>(d) In Akhtar&#x27;s view, what was the reason for his recovery?</p><p>(e) How did the hospital staff treat Manzoor?</p><p>3. Write a paragraph on Manzoor&#x27;s character.</p><p>4. Write the summary of this story in your own words.</p><p>5. Select at least five sentences from this story in which auxiliary verbs are used.</p><p>6. Put diacritics (iʿrāb):</p><p>maflūj, muʿjiza, muʿayyan, masīḥā, marīz, marz, mānind [Urdu words to be vowelled]</p><p>7. Write the autobiography (āp bītī) of a patient admitted to a government hospital.</p><p>8. Put punctuation marks at the appropriate places in the following paragraph.</p><p>In the present age electricity holds the position of a servant in homes factories and offices everywhere it is a necessity of our daily life you pressed a button the fan started the light came on the heater lit up the air-conditioner cooled the room in the refrigerator everything froze the food is ready the clothes are washed and ironed the lift took you up hundreds of feet in short as soon as you press the switch everything happens in a moment [printed without punctuation, to be punctuated]</p><p>9. According to the lesson, put (✓) against the sentences that are correct and (✗) against those that are wrong.</p><p>a. A tremor was upon Akhtar&#x27;s body.</p><p>b. Akhtar and Manzoor were of the same age.</p><p>c. Allah Almighty accepted Akhtar&#x27;s prayer.</p><p>d. Manzoor recovered and went home.</p><p>e. Successful treatment alone ended Akhtar&#x27;s illness.</p><p>f. A frail and emaciated old man lay on Manzoor&#x27;s cot.</p><p>10. Write a story of about four hundred words with the title “Sacrifice and Selflessness (Īsār-o-Qurbānī)”.</p>",
