     "text": "…the man looked at his face, choked with fright, and ran off making strange noises, dropping a bundle. Abdullah, startled too, picked it up: it was hot amritis (sweets). He hurried home and he and his wife ate them with relish. The next night, in drizzle and deeper cold, he waited long in the lane; at last a peanut-seller came, and Abdullah, instead of holding out his hand, said nasally, “Wait a moment, brother!” His frightful face, ghostly voice and the lonely night so terrified the man that he fell senseless; Abdullah calmly tied a seer and a quarter of peanuts in his shawl and went home.",
