   "content": "<p>2. Fill in the blanks:</p><p>(a) He did not have the ________ of keeping up with the times.</p><p>(b) Out of fear his ________ got choked.</p><p>(c) In the cold weather he was sitting outside ________ in the sun.</p><p>(d) ________ boasts is not a good thing.</p><p>(e) The landlord scolded the tenant in harsh ________ .</p><p>3. Explain the following passages with reference to the context: (a) the passage on p.101 beginning “He was so straightforward and guileless that he hardly seemed human…” and ending “…so no one was his friend.”; (b) the passage on p.102 beginning “For three days Master Ilyas sat on his cot with his quilt over his head like an igloo…” and ending “…‘Yes, I was feeling a little cold.’”</p><p>4. Fill in the blanks according to idiomatic usage (rozmarra):</p><p>(a) He came forward grinding his ________ in anger.</p><p>(b) When he heard the news of Pakistan&#x27;s victory he went ________ with joy.</p><p>(c) Dust in your ________ — what ominous things you are saying!</p><p>(d) You have dusted off your ________ and gone after my child.</p><p>(e) I could not watch this frightful scene and out of fear shut my ________ .</p><p>5. Correct the sentences:</p><p>(a) “Our homeland is progressing day by day.” [as printed]</p><p>(b) “He was looking at me with amazement (ḥairāngī).”</p><p>(c) “My heart greatly wishes that I go on Hajj.”</p><p>(d) “I have come to say an important thing to you.”</p><p>(e) “Hearing his cries, people ran to help.”</p><p>6. Put punctuation marks at the appropriate places in the following sentences:</p><p>(a) Whenever you see him he is riding the horse of the wind (building castles in the air)</p><p>(b) The important points of this essay are these</p><p>(c) The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said all human beings are equal</p><p>(d) Boy what are you doing here</p><p>(e) “Not everyone who shakes hands is a friend” — this line of Ahmad Faraz is based on truth</p><p>7. In Urdu the following verbs are used as auxiliary (helping) verbs. With their help make two sentences each in which they are used as auxiliary verbs: dēnā, lēnā, ānā, ḍālnā, jānā, paṛnā, uṭhnā.</p>",
