   "content": "<p>The Conductor — Altaf Fatima</p><p>[Paragraph-wise summary — Altaf Fatima (d. 2018) is in copyright; read the full story in the printed textbook, pp. 107–116.]</p><p>The narrator hears that Lalu has now built a good business in Karachi and a decent bungalow; long ago she had heard, with surprise, that he married a school teacher who accepted an under-matric husband and for years was like the strong wheel — even the steering — of his rickety cart of life. No one’s life runs in a straight line; life is a maze of circles, dead ends and tangled lines, and each must find his own way.</p><p>Lalu was the second son of his family. When he was in class five his progress was slow and disappointing, his features stamped with foolishness, and he stammered so that he said “ṭāf” for kāf and “ḍāf” for gāf; he had learned his whole reader by rote in this way… (continued on p. 108)</p>",
