     "text": "Their common tutor said Lalu knew not a single word and had merely crammed the reader. Lalu’s family lived in the narrator’s small house, its door opening into their courtyard, and the boys studied in the same room. The master despaired of Lalu, and indeed a small child was always perched on his hip, for his mother had decided this was his lot. The master, who wished him well, pulled his ears and rapped his hands: “What will you study? You’ll dig grass; you’ll be your brothers’ and sisters’ servant!” Lalu kept his head down as if he agreed — but when his mother said the same, he smiled sarcastically, glancing sideways, with a mysterious glow on his face, as if some secret were growing within him.",
