     "text": "The doors of his house were open to all, poor and rich, high and low. There was no chamberlain, no doorkeeper, no need to send in a card for an audience, no need of any intermediary for an introduction. Whoever came would pull up a chair and sit down; either he introduced himself or sat silently listening to the talk. When Allama Iqbal paused for a while in his talk, he would turn to him and ask, “Tell me, where have you come from?” He would give his name; if he had some need, he would state it.",
