     "text": "Dr. Muhammad Din Taseer says that one night he was present before Doctor Sahib (Iqbal); some other people were also sitting there when a man whose hair had grown long and who seemed somewhat distraught came, greeted, and sat down. After a while Allama Iqbal turned to him and said, “Tell me, what brings you here?” He said, “I just came to see you.” God knows what Allama Iqbal learned from his face — that he had not eaten, or something else. Anyway he asked, “Will you have something to eat?” He replied, “Yes, please feed me.” Allama Iqbal called Ali Bakhsh and said, “Take him to the other room and give him food.” Hearing this he said, “I will eat right here.” So Ali Bakhsh spread the dining cloth right there and fed him. Even after eating he did not get up and sat on there silently. The night was well advanced, so I left him there and came home. The next day when I presented myself before the Allama, the first question I asked was, “Well, Doctor Sahib, what became of the man who came last night?” He said, “After you left I told him to go to sleep now, but he said he would lie down in your room. So Ali Bakhsh spread a cot for him by the door of my room. Early in the morning he got up and went off somewhere!”",
