     "text": "The late Allama had a great deal of wit in his nature. Even dry philosophical problems he made so interesting with jokes and quips that one wished to sit for hours listening to him. Two or three jokes happened every day, but the quips he made about Sir Shahabuddin have acquired historical standing. It seems that on seeing him nothing but jokes and quips occurred to Allama Iqbal. Sir Shahabuddin’s complexion was dark. Once he came to the Assembly wearing a black suit. When Allama Iqbal saw him, he laughed and said, “Chaudhri Sahib! Today you have come quite naked.”",
