   "content": "<p>Farigh Bukhari</p><p>Born: 1917 · Died: 1997</p><p>Syed Mir Ahmad Shah Bukhari was born in Peshawar. From childhood his nature was spirited. At only thirteen he joined the “Naujawan Bharat Sabha”, which played a militant role in the freedom movement. During the freedom movement and, after the creation of Pakistan, in the struggle for democracy and freedom of expression, he repeatedly endured the hardships of imprisonment.</p><p>He was basically a scholar and poet. He was one of the founders of the Anjuman Taraqqi Pasand Musannifeen (Progressive Writers’ Association). Together with Raza Hamdani he launched the monthly “Sang-e-Meel”. The two wrote many books on Pashto language, literature and culture, including Adabiyat-e-Sarhad, Pashto Lok Geet, Sarhad ke Lok Shair, Pashto Shairi and Pashto Nasr. Zer-o-Bam, Sheeshe ke Pairahan, Khushbu ka Safar, Pyase Hath, Ghazaliya and Bichhra Sawal are collections of his poetry. In 1995 he was honoured with the Presidential Pride of Performance Award.</p><p>Works: Bacha Khan, Album, Barat-e-Ashiqan (prose).</p>",
