     "text": "As a child he was quicksilver and as a youth a whirlwind: whatever road he passed seemed bathed in a rainbow, every gathering was perfumed by his presence, and every garment looked good on him. In old age his fatherly kindness, good manners and sincerity remind the author of the old banyan in the western corner of Shahi Bagh, Peshawar, known as the “tree with seats” because seats had been carved in its trunk where people sheltered from summer sun and winter storms. When it was cut down for some construction the citizens were deeply grieved and still remember it with longing.",
