     "text": "The Khan would not give up the money on any account. At his wits’ end, Bisharat said: forget who is right and who is wrong — remember that our trade will go on in future too; you can make up the shortfall some other time; God forbid, this is not the last deal. The Khan replied that Khan Sang-e-Marjan Khan had advised him: when you meet a friend, meet him as if it were the last meeting — once parted you may never meet again — and when you deal with someone, deal as if it were the last deal. Sheikh Saadi says even a mad dog cannot hope that the one it has bitten will come a second time to be bitten again.",
