   "content": "<p>The Sound of Defeat — Meeraji</p><p>Longings have cast my heart into a strange tangle;</p><p>it thinks that whatever task there is, it is the one to do it.</p><p>It says: let me show new paths to the riders;</p><p>it says: let me bring down the moon-pieces from the sky.</p><p>It says: let me cross the distance of deserts in a moment —</p><p>in truth, it is this conscious feeling I would cross in a moment.</p><p>Let me go and see the new world that lies in the heart of the sea;</p><p>the tale of the stone-forest lies frozen on the mountain’s head.</p><p>It says: let the whole universe become a single speck;</p><p>let the interval that is infinite become just one moment.</p><p>But what of it if intentions are lofty? Lofty intentions</p><p>simple folk have no sense to understand.</p><p>In the world simple people live in great numbers;</p><p>limited is their courage and limited their paths.</p><p>Civilisation and cultures have cast their noose upon them;</p><p>they say: what is to be is only what is bound to be.</p><p>“Changing them, what shall we do with the ways of Nature today?</p><p>Tomorrow the hands of Fate will be upon our skirts.”</p><p>They find comfort in the poverty of the lines drawn before;</p><p>they are lost in the weakness and old age of desire.</p><p>I look at them and they leave their mark on my heart;</p><p>I am one oppressed by the stagnant pull of this environment.</p><p>But yes — in spite of this, there is a blaze in my heart:</p><p>longings have cast my being into a tangle.</p><p>(Paband Nazmen)</p>",
