   "content": "<p>Exercise</p><p>1. Write answers to the following questions according to the given ghazal:</p><p>(a) What is meant by “now blood will speak”?</p><p>(b) What is meant by the wind “listening” (gosh-bar-āwāz)?</p><p>(c) Why were the people of the city silent?</p><p>(d) Why did the poet not tell his last wish?</p><p>2. Write the refrain (radīf) of this ghazal.</p><p>3. Write the rhymes of this ghazal.</p><p>4. In the couplet “Bikne wāloṉ meṉ jahāṉ ek se ek āge ho / aise mele meṉ kharīdār ko kyā bolnā hai”: mentioning something in a text and then bringing in other things related to it — provided they are not opposites — is called murāʿāt-un-naẓīr. In the couplet above, a fair and a buyer are mentioned in keeping with selling. Write at least three couplets in which the figure murāʿāt-un-naẓīr is used.</p><p>5. Explain the following couplet (the maqṭaʿ: “Jahāṉ darbār hoṉ shāhoṉ ke muṣāḥib hoṉ Farāz / wahāṉ Ghālib ke ṭaraf-dār ko kyā bolnā hai”).</p>",
