     "text": "Zafar Iqbal, born in Okara, has a poetic journey of more than half a century. At first he was sometimes near to and sometimes far from the traditions of the ghazal; at last he became free of the spell of the ghazal's traditions, but on this journey he had to pass through hard stages. The common reader and the creative writer of Urdu literature are such captives of the traditions of the Urdu ghazal that they cannot even think of leaving this enchanted atmosphere. In past centuries Hali and Insha did try to break the ghazal's traditions, but what change came to the ghazal through those efforts? Hali and Insha were deprived of their own place in the Urdu ghazal.",
